  "result": "Fixed: `--help` now lists an option's short name first, so you get `-v, --verbose` instead of `--verbose, -v`.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted an option's names by prefix length in reverse, which put the long `--` names before the short `-` ones. I removed `reverse=True`.\n\nI checked it with a small test command, and the test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI left the order of the options themselves alone: they still appear in the order they were declared. Arguments are still listed before options. If the order you meant was one of those, tell me which and I'll look at it.",
